SUMMARY
==========================================================================================
Target's claimed exponent formula: eps^2/(1-eps^2), transition at eps=1
This referee's CORRECTED exponent (from the coefficient-2 fix, adv02):
  2*eps^2/(1-2*eps^2), with the corresponding transition to explosive
  growth at eps=1/sqrt(2) = 0.70711 -- CONFIRMED numerically above (the
  corrected ODE integration becomes non-finite once eps exceeds ~0.707,
  not ~1 as the target's own Sec 5.3 claims).

This means BOTH of Sec 5's headline quantitative findings (the exponent
formula, and the 'sharp qualitative transition at eps=1') are INCORRECT
as literally stated -- though the corrected obstruction is STRICTLY WORSE
(diverges faster, transitions earlier) than what the target reports, so
Sec 6's qualitative negative conclusion is, if anything, reinforced.

